                <pb facs="0835" n="739" sameAs="frus:frus1879/pg739"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure E in Mr. Willard’s dispatch, of October
                        18.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#small-caps">prefecture of the district of
                    magdalena.</hi></head>
                <p>Manuel Moreno, with ten men commissioned by this office, the 27th ultimo, to
                    pursue the criminals whom the prefect of Altar informed me had come into this
                    district, returned on the 1st instant without having been able to arrest them,
                    and only was informed that they had taken the direction of the Sonora River,
                    where it is believed they can be found. All of which I have the honor to inform
                    you in answer to your note of the 26th ultimo.</p>
                <p>Liberty in the constitution.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName>Magdalena</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1878-10-07">October 7,
                        1878</date>.</dateline>
                    <lb/>
                    <signed>JUAN E. DURAN.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>To the <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of State</hi>, <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Ures.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
